th1-surjection-curation-001+math1-bijection-curation-001+math1-union-curation-001+math1-proper-curation-001+math1-complement-curation-001+math1-complement-render-001+math1-division-curation-001+math1-reciprocal-curation-001+math1-inequality-curation-001+math1-inequality-feedback-001+math1-maximum-curation-001+math1-minimum-curation-001+math1-boundedset-curation-001+math1-endpoint-curation-001+audit-groups-20261027+topup-math-i-20261028+topup-math-ii-20261028+topup-pt-20261028+topup-math-iii-20261028+v3-2026-11-02+v3-2026-11-10+v3-2026-11-10+v3-2026-11-10+v3-2026-11-10+type-mix-retire-20261112+type-mix-topup-20261112+type-mix-retire2-20261112+fill-20261112+fill2-20261112","concept_id":"Year-1/1b-Programming-for-EOR/function-call.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/1b-Programming-for-EOR/function-call.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Typing `exp` at the console, without parentheses, prints `function (x)  .Primitive(\"exp\")` instead of a number. Why does R compute nothing?","options":["`exp` has no argument, and R prints the definition whenever one is missing.","R applies `exp` to the last value computed and shows the formula it used.","Without parentheses R shows the function itself; the parentheses make it run.","`exp` is a reserved word that only works inside a larger expression."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7f6811dda681c982e917e6be","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In mathematics $5!=120$. Which line makes R compute this factorial?","options":["`factorial(5)`","`5!`","`factorial[5]`","`factorial 5`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"626e6648db3fb057b8fbe03b","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does R return for `log(1000)`?","options":["`[1] 3`","`[1] 9.965784`","`[1] Inf`","`[1] 6.907755`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"959d0fcbf7fd98bbc66aa406","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does R return for `log(8, 2)`?","options":["`[1] 0.3333333`","`[1] 3`","`[1] 2.079442`","`[1] 0.90309`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"519197e257663b5bec6205d4","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does R return after `n <- 3; factorial(n + 1)`?","options":["`[1] 7`","`[1] 24`","`[1] 6`","an error, since an argument must be a single name or number"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"caeea9aa5e21c4293a90ba06","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which command opens the help page that lists the arguments of `round()` and their defaults?","options":["`round()`","`round`","`?round`","`help(round())`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a6f775378e814a2473a5a03b","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does R return for `sqrt(round(10.6))`?","options":["`[1] 3.316625`","`[1] 3`","`[1] 3.255764`","`[1] 3.162278`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"65b8f61004fb90af4fb19afa","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does R return after `d <- 2; round(7.4567, d)`?","options":["`[1] 7`","`[1] 7.45`","an error, since the number of digits must be typed as a number","`[1] 7.46`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0f672f9c05c7afabda7093de","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does R return for `round(3.14159, sqrt(4))`?","options":["`[1] 3`","`[1] 1.772453`","`[1] 3.14`","`[1] 3.1416`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d3ebd299e33b2c2ac00fa5a8","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which R code computes $\\mathrm{e}^2$?","options":["`e^2`","`exp(2)`","`exp^2`","`log(2)`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"80f5335cf0798eb1b3af19f5","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a positive number `x`, the nested call `exp(sqrt(x))` corresponds to which mathematical expression?","options":["$\\sqrt{\\mathrm{e}^{x}}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{x}\\sqrt{x}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{x}+\\sqrt{x}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{\\sqrt{x}}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"657639726001a09e484c9ecd","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"After `x <- 49`, which line makes `x` hold the value 7?","options":["`x <- sqrt(x)`","`sqrt(x)`","`y <- sqrt(x)`","`x <- sqrt`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d4da6a44156762003e2037d1","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which call returns the natural logarithm of 50 rounded to two decimals, `[1] 3.91`?","options":["`log(round(50, 2))`","`round(log(50, 2))`","`round(log(50), 2)`","`round(log(50))`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a185e8a7db21b82257fdf65f","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What happens when R runs `sqrt(4, 9)`, intending the square roots of 4 and 9?","options":["It returns `[1] 2 3`, the square roots of 4 and of 9 in turn.","It stops: `2 arguments passed to 'sqrt' which requires 1`.","It returns `[1] 3.605551`, the square root of the sum $4+9$.","It returns `[1] 2` and silently ignores the extra value 9."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"703fd5853cfd63ebfbe6a205","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What does R return for `round(sqrt(2), 2)^2`?","options":["`[1] 1.9881`","`[1] 2`","`[1] 1.99`","`[1] 1.41`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"78e2285a065be913f89e09c1","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What does R return for `exp(log(10) / 2)`?","options":["`[1] 5`","`[1] 1.151293`","`[1] 148.4132`","`[1] 3.162278`"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fc21a6f3e2dd444709edb1df","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement correctly compares the nested call `round(sqrt(10), 2)` with the two lines `s <- sqrt(10); round(s, 2)`?","options":["The nested call runs `round()` first and `sqrt()` second, so it gives a different value.","Both give 3.16; the nested call passes the value of `sqrt(10)` on without naming it.","The two-line version is less precise, since `s` keeps only the digits R prints for it.","Only the two-line version works, since an argument must be a name or a number."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9a703dfd7960ca212f11347e","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"What does R give for `sqrt(log(0.5))`?","options":["`[1] NaN`, with the warning `NaNs produced`","`[1] -0.3465736`","`[1] 0.8325546`","the error `NaNs produced`, which stops the calculation"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4828e7b75fe402cdb2d59623","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"What happens when R runs `round(sqrt(\"16\"), 1)`?","options":["It returns `[1] 4`, after reading the text `\"16\"` as the number 16.","It returns `[1] NA` with a warning, and `round()` passes the `NA` on.","It stops with `non-numeric argument to mathematical function` from `sqrt()`.","It returns `[1] \"4\"`, keeping the result as text like the input."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1f045722292aa640b19dddd6","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1b_programming_for_eor_function_call_fb76c7dc_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"What happens when R runs `f <- sqrt; f(49)`, where `sqrt` is written without parentheses?","options":["It stops at `f(49)` with `could not find function \"f\"`.","It stops at `f <- sqrt`, since `sqrt` needs an argument before it can be stored.","It prints `function (x)  .Primitive(\"sqrt\")`, the object stored in `f`.","It returns `[1] 7`: `f` holds the function `sqrt`, and the parentheses run it."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"19093a1470d4db299187cd3d","time_limit":40}]}}